From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000036 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mortyzhaoyu <morty.zhaoyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 17:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: rockchip: support BSP iommu-v2 nodes (compatible +
 clocks)

The RK3576 BSP multimedia devicetree declares the MPP/RGA/NPU MMUs as
"rockchip,iommu-v2", which the vendor 6.1 driver binds with the same v2
ops as "rockchip,rk3568-iommu". Add the compatible so those MMUs probe
on mainline.

The vendor driver also acquires clocks with devm_clk_bulk_get_all()
while mainline requires clocks named "aclk"/"iface". BSP nodes break
that assumption: rknpu_mmu uses "aclk0"/"aclk1"/"a_iface"/"h_iface" and
jpeg_mmu misspells the property as "clock-name". With named lookup both
MMUs probed with zero clocks and the first register access on an
ungated clock hung the bus right after the mpp-iep2 probe. Switch to
devm_clk_bulk_get_all() to match vendor behaviour.

Signed-off-by: mortyzhaoyu <morty.zhaoyu@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c | 39 +++++++++++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
@@ -93,11 +93,6 @@
 	struct iommu_domain domain;
 };
 
-/* list of clocks required by IOMMU */
-static const char * const rk_iommu_clocks[] = {
-	"aclk", "iface",
-};
-
 struct rk_iommu_ops {
 	phys_addr_t (*pt_address)(u32 dte);
 	u32 (*mk_dtentries)(dma_addr_t pt_dma);
@@ -1365,25 +1360,20 @@
 	iommu->reset_disabled = device_property_read_bool(dev,
 					"rockchip,disable-mmu-reset");
 
-	iommu->num_clocks = ARRAY_SIZE(rk_iommu_clocks);
-	iommu->clocks = devm_kcalloc(iommu->dev, iommu->num_clocks,
-				     sizeof(*iommu->clocks), GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!iommu->clocks)
-		return -ENOMEM;
-
-	for (i = 0; i < iommu->num_clocks; ++i)
-		iommu->clocks[i].id = rk_iommu_clocks[i];
-
 	/*
-	 * iommu clocks should be present for all new devices and devicetrees
-	 * but there are older devicetrees without clocks out in the wild.
-	 * So clocks as optional for the time being.
+	 * Rockchip BSP devicetrees (e.g. the RK3576 multimedia block) carry
+	 * IOMMU clocks under non-standard names ("aclk0"/"aclk1"/... on
+	 * rknpu_mmu) or with a broken "clock-name" property (jpeg_mmu).
+	 * Match the vendor driver and grab all clocks regardless of names;
+	 * clocks stay optional for old devicetrees without any.
 	 */
-	err = devm_clk_bulk_get(iommu->dev, iommu->num_clocks, iommu->clocks);
+	err = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(iommu->dev, &iommu->clocks);
 	if (err == -ENOENT)
 		iommu->num_clocks = 0;
-	else if (err)
+	else if (err < 0)
 		return err;
+	else
+		iommu->num_clocks = err;
 
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare(iommu->num_clocks, iommu->clocks);
 	if (err)
@@ -1488,6 +1478,10 @@
 	{	.compatible = "rockchip,rk3568-iommu",
 		.data = &iommu_data_ops_v2,
 	},
+	/* Rockchip BSP devicetrees (RK3576/RK3588 multimedia) use this name */
+	{	.compatible = "rockchip,iommu-v2",
+		.data = &iommu_data_ops_v2,
+	},
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
 
